Sharding limitations

Operational restrictions for sharding
mongodb does not support unique index across shards
except when the unique index contains the full shard key as a prefix of the index
mongodb does not guarantee consistent indexes across shards

jumbo chunks - when there's just one index and cannot be split further. jumbo chunks grow unbounded

fix:
identify jumbo chunk - sh.status(), 
split the jumbo chunk manually - sh.splitAt()
increase chunk size - if splitting is not feasible, temporarily increase max size to improve distribution db.settings.update()
if chunk is beyond splitting, consider refining or resharding
take off jumbo flag
rebalance chunks - sh.startBalancer() trigger a manual rebalancing of chunks across shards

top chunk - becomes bottleneck

Scatter gather queries - A scatter-gather query is a query in a MongoDB sharded cluster that mongos sends to multiple or all shards, then gathers and merges their results before returning them to the client









































